 "purpose": "The clock topic: reading and setting an analogue clock, times in Flemish words, the 24-hour notation, and later and earlier.",
 "details": "A time is everywhere a number of minutes after midnight (0 to 1439), as in grootheden.py; an analogue clock shows only 12 hours, so 3.15 and 15.15 count as equal there (nakijken compares modulo 720, except for 24-hour and later/earlier questions). Helpers write times as Flemish words (woorden, e.g. 'vijf voor half vier') and read them back (lees_woorden), name the part of the day (dagdeel), and describe how to read the long hand (lange_wijzer). The one topic Klok makes seven kinds: lezen (read the clock; clock window or drawn clock), woorden_naar and naar_woorden, zetten (set the hands; input kind 'wijzers'), 24uur, later and vroeger. The klad is on only for later, earlier and 24 hours. The window and drawing of the clock are in venster/klokbeeld.py, venster/klokvenster.py and terminal/modellen.py.",
 "module_docstring": "De klok: een wijzerklok lezen en zetten, tijden in Vlaamse woorden, de 24-uursnotatie, later en vroeger.",
